=== THE DIVERGENCE PROBLEM: the same file must differ per host

=== back on host 1: pull the other host's commit
MERGE CONFLICT, which is the whole problem:
    | Auto-merging .bashrc
    | CONFLICT (content): Merge conflict in .bashrc
    | Automatic merge failed; fix conflicts and then commit the result.

  .bashrc now contains conflict markers:
    | <<<<<<< HEAD
    | export PATH="/opt/homebrew/bin:$PATH"
    | alias ll="ls -lG"
    | =======
    | export PATH="/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:$PATH"
    | >>>>>>> origin/master

  Nothing here is a mistake. Both edits are correct FOR THEIR HOST.
  Plain git has no way to say 'this line is per-OS', so every sync
  re-litigates it. That is the gap tools like chezmoi/yadm fill.

